# http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/skg-if/extension/srv/ontology/Service> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/skg-if/extension/srv/ontology/APIProfile> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "In SKG-IF, it is used in the following classes (domain):\n\n* srv:Service\n\nIn SKG-IF, it is used to link a Service to an APIProfile instance describing endpoint and API specifications.\n* srv:APIProfile" .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dcterms:conformsTo (SKG-IF labels: srv_api_profile)" .
# 
# http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "In SKG-IF, it is used in the following classes (domain):\n* srv:Service\n* fabio:Work\n\nIn SKG-IF, it is used to link to entities belonging to the following classes (range):\n* foaf:Organization" .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Generic queryable index of all organisations associated with a Service. The specific properties srv:hasHostingOrganisation, srv:hasHostingLegalEntity, and srv:isPartOfResearchInfrastructure are semantically narrower and are intended to be declared rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:relation once the ontology is finalised. Until those subproperty axioms are added, data producers must explicitly copy the local_identifier of each organisation referenced in those specific properties into this field, so that generic organisation queries against relevant_organisations remain complete." .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dcterms:relation (SKG-IF labels: relevant_organisations)" .
# 
# http://purl.org/dc/terms/scope
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/scope> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
# 
# http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "In SKG-IF, it is used in the following classes (domain):\n* dcat:DataService\n* srv:Service\n\nIn SKG-IF, it is used to link to entities belonging to the following classes (range):\n* owl:Thing" .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Library of Congress Classification code IRI for the discipline of the Service. Use the 'all' shortcut (→ loc:classification) for discipline-agnostic services." .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dcterms:subject (SKG-IF labels: disciplines)" .
# 
# http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/skg-if/extension/srv/ontology/Service> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "In SKG-IF, it is used in the following classes (domain):\n* fabio:Work\n* srv:Service\n\nIn SKG-IF, it is used to link to entities belonging to the following classes (range):\n* bido:BibliometricDataInTime" .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The core SKG-IF ontology restricts this property's domain to fabio:Work (research products).\nThis entry extends effective use to srv:Service, following the same pragmatic usage already present\nin all 120+ ext-srv example files.\nNOTE: The full BIDO structure (bido:holdsBibliometricDataInTime → bido:BibliometricDataInTime →\nbido:withBibliometricData → fabio:SubjectTerm) is overkill for Service topic classification.\nThe bido:BibliometricDataInTime wrapper exists to carry provenance (trust scores from multiple\ninference systems) and temporal tracking — neither of which applies to services, where topics\nare asserted directly by the service maintainer. Kept for consistency with the core inter-entity\nrelation pattern between entities and Topic entities (both must resolve via the same local_identifier).\nTODO: Propose to the core team (skg-if/data-model) that bido:holdsBibliometricDataInTime be\nbroadened to a general cross-entity alias not restricted to fabio:Work — topics are equally\napplicable to Services, Venues, Data Sources, etc. Consider also whether a simpler cross-entity\ntopics relation (without the BIDO provenance wrapper) would better serve non-bibliometric entities." .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/spar/bido/> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/holdsBibliometricDataInTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "bido:holdsBibliometricDataInTime (SKG-IF labels: topics)" .
# 
# http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://purl.org/spar/bido/BibliometricDataInTime> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://purl.org/spar/fabio/SubjectTerm> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "In SKG-IF, it is used in the following classes (domain):\n* bido:BibliometricDataInTime\n\nIn SKG-IF, it is used to link to entities belonging to the following classes (range):\n* fabio:SubjectTerm" .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a bido:BibliometricDataInTime wrapper node to the fabio:SubjectTerm (Topic) it carries." .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/spar/bido/> .
<http://purl.org/spar/bido/withBibliometricData> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "bido:withBibliometricData (SKG-IF labels: term)" .
